dill will be a COMPLETE Replacement for paru or yay or alternatives
    it is designed so it feels familiar to both arch users ie dill -Syu updates, or for ex-debian users dill update etc
it is replacing pickles-update
it is designed to be modular, for ease of use, updates, and mod adding
It is designed with ease of use, by both Expert Arch users, and Debian users moving to Arch
dill should have some "Aussie Bogan" humor, With an R18+ rating, can be crude, can swear, Definately sarcastic


We are creating a Complete package which in a standard arch install will be installed to /usr/lib/dill/ 
with symlinks in /usr/bin(/dill/) to dill , and eventually dill-tui & dill-gui

dill is the bin/executable for dill It contains the redirections
dill.config is the user changeable config
dill-gui and dill-tui are placeholders for futute updates, Can be edited for ideas

pickles-update.sh Is to enform previous pickles-update users about change to dill, and show dill help or man package

dill.config is to be used for User editable config (some examples in already)
Scripts should first check ~/.config/dill/dill.config, and if it doesn't exist use /usr/lib/dill/dill.config
.md files should be self explanatory

scripts folder scripts/ equates to /usr/lib/dill/scripts/

Scripts in scripts/ Are for modules

